  "result": "I fixed the option order in `--help`. Options with both a short and a long name now list the short one first, as in `-a, --alpha`. Before, the output read `--alpha, -a`.\n\nThe cause was in `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py`. It sorted option names by prefix length in reverse, which put `--long` ahead of `-s`. I removed `reverse=True`.\n\nI added `test_join_options_short_first` to `tests/test_formatting.py`. The full suite passes, with 1907 passed and 102 skipped. I ran the original repro before the fix. I didn't re-run it after the edit, so only the new test checks the corrected order.\n\nI took \"weird order\" to mean this short/long ordering. The order of the options themselves matches declaration order, so I left that alone. If you meant something else, send me the output you're seeing.",
